// The settlement lifecycle of a robocall's payment. A robocall is authorized
// (a hold placed on the estimate) before it dials, then captured for the ACTUAL
// billable count once CallHub reports it — hold + capture-actual, not
// prepay-on-estimate. Terminal states cover the ways a hold ends: captured/
// charged (money taken), voided/cancelled (hold released, no charge), disputed/
// uncollectable (money owed but not collected). The hold and settlement
// transitions themselves land in later slices; this slice only seeds
// pending_payment.
enum RobocallSettleState {
  pending_payment
  authorized
  settling
  captured
  charged
  voided
  cancelled
  disputed
  uncollectable
  // The single-owner claim held while the pay-time Stripe hold is in flight, and
  // the terminal for a declined card. Appended (not slotted between
  // pending_payment and authorized) so the enum order matches what the
  // append-only ADD VALUE migration produces.
  hold_pending
  hold_failed
  // The single-owner claim held while an authorized draft's CallHub voice-
  // broadcast campaign is being staged (created PAUSED, not dialed). Transient:
  // a successful stage releases the row back to authorized with its CallHub
  // campaign pk_str set. Appended for the same append-only ADD VALUE reason.
  staging
  // The single-owner claim held while the send slice launches (STARTs) the
  // staged CallHub campaign — the transient state that guards against dialing
  // the same run twice. `dialed` is the terminal once the launch has committed
  // and the broadcast is dialing, awaiting completion. Both appended for the
  // same append-only ADD VALUE reason.
  dialing
  dialed
  // The single-owner claim held while the capture slice captures the authorized
  // hold for the actual completed-call count — the guard against capturing the
  // same run twice. A successful capture advances to `captured`; a lapsed hold
  // to `uncollectable`; a zero-billable run to `voided`. Appended for the same
  // append-only ADD VALUE reason.
  capturing
  // The single-owner claim held while the fresh-charge recovery charges a
  // delivered run whose authorization hold lapsed (an off-session charge, NOT a
  // hold capture) — the guard against charging the same run twice. A successful
  // charge advances to `charged`; a declined card returns to `uncollectable`
  // (chargeIntentId set, so it is not re-attempted). Appended for the same
  // append-only ADD VALUE reason.
  charging
  // Terminal for a robocall the send chain could NOT deliver, reached ONLY
  // pre-dial: a PERMANENT CallHub staging or send failure (a non-recoverable
  // 4xx). The authorization hold is voided (no calls were placed, so no charge),
  // the spine flips to `failed`, and the candidate is emailed (SendFailed).
  // Distinct from `uncollectable`, a DELIVERED run we could not capture — a
  // completion-poll failure on a dialed run goes there, never here. Appended for
  // the same append-only ADD VALUE reason.
  send_failed
  // CONTINGENCY upfront-charge billing (robocall-estimate-billing branch, never
  // main). `paid` is the success terminal for a robocall whose ESTIMATE was
  // charged in full up front (no hold, no capture-actual): it is what the staging
  // and send sweeps key on to stage + dial on this branch, exactly where the
  // hold model keyed on `authorized`. `charge_failed` is the declined-card
  // terminal (mirrors `hold_failed`). Both appended for the same append-only ADD
  // VALUE reason. Estimate-billed rows never enter the hold/settlement states
  // (hold_pending/authorized/settling/capturing/uncollectable/…), so the
  // capture-side sweeps no-op on them.
  paid
  charge_failed
}

model OutreachRobocall {
  id             Int      @id @default(autoincrement())
  createdAt      DateTime @default(now()) @map("created_at")
  updatedAt      DateTime @updatedAt @map("updated_at")
  outreach       Outreach @relation(fields: [outreachId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  outreachId     Int      @unique @map("outreach_id")
  // The recorded audio's S3 object key (bucket ROBOCALL_AUDIO_BUCKET), persisted
  // at draft so the later slices are self-contained when the browser is gone.
  // Unique: a fresh per-recording key is one intended send, so the constraint
  // is the atomic backstop that makes a concurrent double-submit fail the second
  // INSERT rather than mint a second billable anchor.
  audioKey       String   @unique @map("audio_key")
  // The rented CallHub caller-ID number the candidate reads aloud as the
  // callback; held through payment for the later send slice to dial from.
  callbackNumber String   @map("callback_number")
  // Server-derived landline count at draft time (the audience's hasLandline
  // reachable count). A snapshot for the record and the pay-step estimate — the
  // amount actually captured is re-derived from CallHub's dialed count later.
  billableCount  Int      @map("billable_count")
  // The authorized estimate, in cents — what the hold is placed for. The
  // captured amount can be less once the actual dialed count is known.
  amountInCents  Int      @map("amount_in_cents")

  // --- payment / settlement state (populated by later slices) -------------

  // The Stripe customer the hold and capture run against.
  stripeCustomerId       String?             @map("stripe_customer_id")
  // The saved card the hold and capture charge.
  paymentMethodId        String?             @map("payment_method_id")
  // The CallHub voice-broadcast campaign this robocall dials from (its PK, as a
  // string — CallHub ids exceed a 32-bit int).
  callhubCampaignPkStr   String?             @map("callhub_campaign_pk_str")
  // The CallHub campaign's scheduled dial window, mirrored back for settlement.
  callhubStartingDate    DateTime?           @map("callhub_starting_date")
  callhubExpirationDate  DateTime?           @map("callhub_expiration_date")
  // The Stripe PaymentIntent the hold is placed on (manual capture).
  authorizationIntentId  String?             @map("authorization_intent_id")
  // The amount actually authorized on the hold, in cents.
  authorizedAmountInCents Int?               @map("authorized_amount_in_cents")
  // The deadline by which the hold must be captured before Stripe auto-expires
  // it (Stripe holds last ~7 days).
  captureBefore          DateTime?           @map("capture_before")
  // The amount actually captured off the hold once the dialed count is known.
  capturedAmountInCents  Int?                @map("captured_amount_in_cents")
  // The Stripe PaymentIntent a fresh charge is placed on when the hold has
  // lapsed and a new charge is needed instead of a capture.
  chargeIntentId         String?             @map("charge_intent_id")
  // How many times settlement has been attempted, to bound retries.
  payAttempt             Int                 @default(0) @map("pay_attempt")
  // When the CallHub voice-broadcast was launched (START). Stamped by the send
  // slice at the dialing → dialed commit; null until the run actually dials.
  dialedAt               DateTime?           @map("dialed_at")
  // Set true when the send slice confirmed a PERMANENT CallHub launch rejection
  // (a definitive 4xx — the campaign is guaranteed still PAUSED, never dialed)
  // but could not immediately commit the send_failed terminal (e.g. a transient
  // DB error inside failSend). Persisting the fact is what lets the stale-dialing
  // sweep FAIL the send instead of reading a still-PAUSED campaign as a transient
  // strand, reverting to `authorized`, and relaunching into the same 4xx forever.
  // Only ever read while the row is still `dialing`; a send_failed row is
  // terminal, so a lingering true value on it is inert.
  permanentSendFailure   Boolean             @default(false) @map("permanent_send_failure")
  // When this draft's audio passed the server-side compliance check, mirrored
  // from the RobocallComplianceResult at create. A hard prerequisite for
  // dialing: the send slice refuses to launch a draft whose value is null, a
  // belt-and-suspenders backstop under the create-time gate.
  compliancePassedAt     DateTime?           @map("compliance_passed_at")
  // The S3 ETag of the audio that passed compliance, FROZEN at create from the
  // RobocallComplianceResult. The staging step re-reads the object's current
  // ETag before uploading it to CallHub and refuses a mismatch, so bytes swapped
  // after the create gate (a re-upload to the same presigned key) can never
  // reach voters. Frozen on the draft — not re-read from the mutable verdict —
  // so re-running compliance on swapped bytes can't retroactively bless them.
  complianceAudioEtag    String?             @map("compliance_audio_etag")
  // When the last "fix your card" reminder was sent for a hold_failed draft.
  // The daily reminder sweep stamps this on emit and only re-reminds a draft
  // whose value is null or older than ~1 day, so it is the primary once/day
  // guard against a double sweep re-emailing.
  lastReminderSentAt     DateTime?           @map("last_reminder_sent_at")
  // The completion sweep's snapshot of CallHub's actual completed/billable call
  // count (credits_usage `voice_calls`). Written on each terminal-status poll so
  // one sweep pass never settles a still-moving count: settlement requires two
  // consecutive polls to read the SAME count. The value the capture slice
  // charges (min(actual, authorized)); null until the run finishes dialing.
  completedCallCount     Int?                @map("completed_call_count")
  // When the completion sweep last polled CallHub for this run's count.
  completionPolledAt     DateTime?           @map("completion_polled_at")
  settleState            RobocallSettleState @default(pending_payment) @map("settle_state")

  @@map("outreach_robocall")
}
